{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-76970705-c5b8-4dd9-83f3-67f5c24facd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-845d9da4bde48239","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-gdlqtd01/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the two administrator-facing reports in the RHOAI web console that surface idle and stale resources per project: an idle-workbench report sourced from the notebook controller's existing activity tracking, and a stale pipeline-run report sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. It also delivers CSV export of either report. No code changes are made to the notebook controller or Kubeflow Pipelines — both are consumed as read-only data sources.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a per-project idle-workbench report to the web console showing, for each workbench: last activity (from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources (volumes and compute reservations).\n- Add a per-project stale pipeline-run report showing completed runs older than a configurable age threshold, together with their retained artifacts.\n- Make the staleness age threshold administratively configurable without code changes.\n- Add a CSV export action for either report, producing the same columns shown in the console.\n- Validate report correctness against the source systems: idle-workbench values must match the notebook controller's tracked activity data, and stale-run values must match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata (this is the validation of the passive components, which receive no code changes).\n- Explicitly excluded per the strategy's Out of Scope: automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and cost/chargeback calculations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given a project with workbenches, the web console renders an idle-workbench report listing each workbench with its last activity, owner, and reserved resources, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n2. Given a project with completed pipeline runs, the web console renders a stale pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than the configured age threshold with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n3. The staleness age threshold is configurable by an administrator without code changes, and the stale-run report reflects a changed threshold.\n4. For a sample project, every value in the idle-workbench report matches the notebook controller's activity-tracking data, and every value in the stale pipeline-run report matches the Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata for the same project.\n5. An administrator can export either report as CSV, and the exported CSV contains the same rows and columns as the report displayed in the console.\n6. The delivered feature performs no automated reclamation or deletion of resources and computes no cost or chargeback values.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook controller activity tracking — covered by Scope items 1 and 4, ACs 1 and 4.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata — covered by Scope items 2-3, ACs 2, 3 and 4.\n- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)**: CSV export of either report — covered by Scope item 4 and AC 5. Bundled because the export is an action on the same report surfaces and reads the same report data; a separate epic would rebuild the same views and data paths.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28554,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b302c4c03b6016e6","agent_id":"a18bae22e2e763d72","session_