hen/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Decomposition proceeded from the HLR table, Affected Components list, and Out of Scope. Team assignments were taken from the architecture context owning teams.\n60\t- **E002 team assumption:** with no Impacted Teams table, the documentation epic is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard team (the feature owner). If documentation is owned by a separate docs team, reassign E002 before scheduling.\n61\t- **HLR-3 bundling:** CSV export (P2) is bundled into E001 — see the traceability row above for the rationale.\n62\t- **No priority inversions detected:** P1 for both reports (the core admin value), P2 for export and docs is consistent with the strategy's stated priorities.\n63\t- **No scope traps detected:** Out of Scope explicitly excludes automated reclamation and cost/chargeback, and no NFR contradicts it. The configurable staleness age has an existing configuration surface (dashboard.md documents per-component defaults via the OdhDashboardConfig CR).\n64\t\n65\t## Tiered Delivery\n66\t\n67\tNot applicable — there are no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all data sources are in-platform and GA.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0659a1e84d8a6c4","agent_id":"ad7c50bb88bf092d2","session_id":"f85c7355-3df5-4b14-a439-1adff2ae9aec","uuid":"76fcd08e-52fb-42e5-9571-8239e509dbe9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:58:57.702Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-acc93c3debf10014","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
