tion steps: how an administrator can manually stop or remove idle workbenches and clean up stale pipeline runs and their artifacts, with appropriate cautions — written to match the implementation, which performs no automated reclamation.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t1. Published documentation explains both reports — the idle-workbench report and the stale pipeline-run report — including the meaning of each reported field and the data source behind it.\n49\t2. Published documentation explains how to configure the staleness age threshold and how to export either report as CSV.\n50\t3. Published documentation provides step-by-step safe reclamation guidance for idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, clearly framed as manual actions (no automated reclamation).\n51\t4. The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports and accurately reflects the shipped behavior, including any configuration defaults.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps — covered by all Scope items and ACs 1-4.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0659a1e84d8a6c4","agent_id":"ad7c50bb88bf092d2","session_id":"f85c7355-3df5-4b14-a439-1adff2ae9aec","uuid":"de099722-5394-4ddc-bc5f-6e21f856a059","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:59:00.701Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b463c72050dab4b1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
